R2.3 STANDING SEMANTIC-DELEGATION AUTHORITY — CONSOLIDATED CURRENT BOUNDARY.

Preserve all previously approved R2.3 permissions, restrictions, immutable source contracts, authority boundaries and audit history. This instruction consolidates the standing delegation already granted for isolated feature000 formal/reference R2.3 work and extends it to the current MISSING_CONCRETE_SEED_EVIDENCE_VERIFIER boundary.

It does not reopen R1/R2.1/R2.2, does not authorize production integration or full R3, and does not itself establish R2.3 closure, recovery correctness or Formal GO.

The orchestrator is authorized to design, select, implement, prove, review and qualify the minimal deterministic formal/reference contracts necessary to complete the already authorized R2.3 source/recovery relation without returning for another human decision merely because another missing binding, representation, persistence association or deterministic verifier must be made explicit.

This standing authority includes both:

1. the previously delegated persistence/durability/source-association class, including EC_DURABLE_COMMIT_BINDING_NOT_SELECTED; and
2. the current MISSING_CONCRETE_SEED_EVIDENCE_VERIFIER class, subject to the authority limits below.

For these delegated classes, prior instructions requiring a specification-only document followed by STOP and a second human semantic-selection decision are superseded. The orchestrator must still record every selected contract explicitly and immutably before relying on it, but it need not request another Pending decision if the selected solution remains completely inside this authority envelope.

GENERAL DELEGATED R2.3 AUTHORITY

Within isolated feature000 formal/reference R2.3, the orchestrator may:

- inspect and compose all already approved immutable contracts and exact original-source evidence;
- determine that an existing approved contract applies where an explicit applicability argument establishes that fact;
- when existing approved contracts underdetermine a required R2.3 relation, select one minimal deterministic future-generation formal/reference contract using already approved authority;
- introduce the minimum formal/reference fields, schema versions, canonical encodings, identifiers, hashes, source relations, guards and proof machinery necessary to express that contract;
- implement codecs, parsers, checkers, source validators, model guards, fixtures, generators and formal/reference tests required by that contract;
- construct Lean/TLA/refinement proofs and supporting helper lemmas;
- revise technical details when proof, review or qualification reveals an error, provided the corrected semantics remain inside this authority envelope;
- perform ordinary technical decomposition without further human approval;
- run applicable source/model/refinement/mutant/compatibility/qualification gates and ordinary two-process reviews;
- continue R2.3 composition after successful component qualification instead of stopping merely because an intermediate contract or component has been completed.

Every delegated semantic resolution must be explicit, immutable-source-bound and auditable. Record exact source inputs, selected rule, materially relevant alternatives, rationale, compatibility consequences, affected source/model/reference/proof artifacts and qualification evidence.

A semantic choice must not be hidden inside a theorem premise, helper definition, trusted callback, generated fixture, prevalidated input or opaque success predicate.

EC PERSISTENCE / DURABILITY DELEGATION

For the already identified EC persistence/durability boundary, the orchestrator may within the isolated formal/reference model:

- define the exact persisted formal/reference object binding original E/seed bytes, original event/cut and complete computed P0/P1;
- select exact canonical formal/reference bytes, identifiers, hashes, schema fields/versions and source relations necessary for that binding;
- define append, durability barrier, commit and expose ordering using already approved storage/durability authority and primitives;
- define deterministic incomplete/crash/replay/conflict interpretation;
- preserve and formally bind original physical slots, public vote ordinals, object identities, retries, every retained source occurrence and complete lineage;
- introduce the minimum isolated formal/reference persistence envelope or record representation needed to express and prove that semantics;
- implement and qualify its codecs/checkers/model guards/fixtures/Lean/TLA/refinement machinery;
- select among multiple admissible representations the minimal deterministic alternative that reuses the greatest amount of already approved authority and does not claim legacy production compatibility.

The orchestrator does not need another Pending decision merely because the selected formal/reference persistence representation or byte layout did not previously exist.

MISSING_CONCRETE_SEED_EVIDENCE_VERIFIER DELEGATION

The existing checkpoint 46f5acff seed-source audit establishes the current boundary for this work. Reuse its exact immutable corpus/source references; do not repeat the same audit without substantive new evidence.

The orchestrator is authorized to design, select, implement, prove and qualify the minimal deterministic concrete seed evidence verifier and seed derivation/source-binding contract necessary to discharge MISSING_CONCRETE_SEED_EVIDENCE_VERIFIER, without another human Pending decision, provided the selected contract uses only already approved authority and remains within the limits below.

Within this seed delegation the orchestrator may:

- bind exact original reveal/beacon/transcript evidence bytes and every retained source occurrence to the already approved fixed-epoch enrolled Snapshot Provenance Profile v1;
- define exact original accepted seed evidence/transcript fields;
- define canonical/signable preimages and domain separation;
- define exact context binding to the original validator epoch, ISC consensus body b, round/context and original event/cut;
- reuse already approved validator/epoch/ISC/configuration authority and already independently authenticated keys where an explicit applicability argument establishes that their approved semantics cover seed evidence verification;
- define the deterministic verification algorithm;
- define deterministic evidence acceptance, selection, ordering and duplicate handling;
- define missing, invalid and incomplete evidence behavior without excluding lawful histories;
- define the exact deterministic seed_id derivation from already authorized original evidence and context;
- preserve every original signer/object/cut/history occurrence and complete downstream lineage;
- introduce the minimum isolated formal/reference schema fields, canonical encodings, hashes, codecs, checkers, model guards, fixtures and Lean/TLA/refinement machinery required to implement and prove that rule;
- select among multiple admissible seed-verifier designs the minimal deterministic contract that introduces the least new semantics and maximally reuses already approved authority;
- revise technical details if proof or review reveals an error, provided the corrected contract remains inside this authority envelope;
- run applicable source/model/refinement/mutant/compatibility gates and ordinary two-process reviews and then continue R2.3 composition.

No separate Pending decision is required merely because the selected seed verifier, preimage format or deterministic seed derivation rule did not previously exist, provided it uses only already approved authority, original evidence and fixed context described above.

For the selected seed contract, immutable evidence must record at minimum:

- exact original source bytes/types;
- key/profile applicability;
- verification algorithm;
- canonical/signable preimage and domain separation;
- epoch/ISC/round/context/event-cut binding;
- seed derivation algorithm;
- acceptance/selection/order/duplicate behavior;
- missing/invalid/incomplete behavior;
- materially relevant alternatives and selection rationale;
- compatibility consequences;
- affected theorem/model/reference/qualification obligations.

Do not use public ExpectedSeedValue, a successful downstream EC, successful FinalizeEC/Next, custody, hash equality, TLS transport, durable=true, a supplied certificate or another downstream-success observation as its own independent seed authority or verifier.

AUTHORITY ENVELOPE — NEW HUMAN DECISION REQUIRED OUTSIDE IT

A new Pending decision is mandatory before any action that would:

- introduce a new trust or authority root;
- introduce a new independently trusted key source;
- introduce a new signing authority or signing protocol whose existing approved authority does not already cover the required use;
- introduce a new beacon authority, entropy authority or independent source-of-truth service;
- introduce a factual-history observer or new physical-history source of truth;
- silently repurpose an existing authority or key whose approved contract does not cover the new use;
- weaken validator membership/epoch authentication requirements;
- weaken or narrow the approved source/admissible-history domain;
- exclude missing, invalid, duplicate or incomplete original evidence merely to make a proof succeed;
- invent source caps or erase loss/fault/history cases;
- synthesize, discard, truncate, relabel or replace missing original bytes/history with callbacks, fixtures or successful downstream results;
- change Snapshot Provenance Profile v1, EC-SOURCE-STEP-v1, Arithmetic Unit Source Binding v1 or another already selected semantic contract rather than compose the minimum missing binding;
- change existing seed, certificate, QC, signature, validator, storage-authority, WAL or original-object identity rules beyond consequences already entailed by approved contracts;
- change deployed legacy production semantics or production Init/Next;
- add or change a production WAL record kind;
- add or change production WAL/storage byte encoding;
- claim existing legacy histories conform to a future-generation formal/reference contract without independently established evidence;
- choose a concrete production seed, private key, arithmetic quantum, sigma or other deployment/runtime semantic value;
- introduce a new clock, duration, expiry mechanism, external oracle, network-bootstrap authority, backup authority, membership change or epoch change;
- enable production C++/ABI/Java/sidecar integration, production recovery deployment or arithmetic guard removal;
- weaken any safety, determinism, source-provenance, compatibility, recovery, review or Formal GO gate;
- reopen R1/R2.1/R2.2 outside their already approved original domains;
- change the mandatory R2.3 closure criterion;
- weaken or alter the required substantive content of DeltaReduce.nativeArithmeticRecoveryRefines;
- enter full R3.

Where several candidate contracts remain possible inside this envelope, the orchestrator is authorized to select the minimal deterministic contract that:

1. introduces the least new semantics;
2. reuses the greatest amount of already approved authority and canonical representation;
3. preserves the largest lawful source/history domain;
4. adds the smallest isolated formal/reference surface;
5. does not claim legacy or production compatibility without independent evidence.

The selected alternative and rationale must be recorded in immutable evidence; selection inside this envelope does not require another human decision.

EXECUTION AND CLOSURE RULES

R2.3 remains OPEN until its complete source/state relation, initial/incomplete/ABORT correspondence, retained-history obligations, affected models, proofs and required reviews substantively succeed.

A component PASS, process review, ACK, scope application or delegated semantic selection is not R2.3 closure and is not Formal GO.

R1/R2.1/R2.2 remain CLOSED only for their already established original domains.

No sorry, hidden/circular/public-success axioms, vacuous theorem/domain weakening, opaque accept callbacks or relabelled FAIL/NO_GO are permitted.

Requalify every affected source/model/refinement/mutant/compatibility/review gate required by the resulting semantics. Sequential process reviews are not independent Formal GO attestations.

After substantive reviewed R2.3 closure, continue the already authorized DeltaReduce.nativeArithmeticRecoveryRefines, its axiom audit and applicable formal/refinement/mutant/compatibility/qualification gates.

Full R3 remains forbidden.

Preserve the existing sprint, graph history, assignment/review history, immutable evidence, frozen references and all unrelated files. No reimport, reset, manual graph advancement, fake RESUME/START, duplicate result/review, nginx-qa patch/deploy/restart or other runtime-state manipulation is authorized by this semantic delegation.

ACK changes scope authorization/audit only; it never completes an assignment, approves a review, advances the graph or bypasses another gate.

Retained restrictions:
- No production C++/ABI/Java/sidecar integration, production recovery deployment or arithmetic guard removal; exact compatible merged Formal GO remains required. Future feature000 semantic/model changes are only those permitted by the current standing R2.3 semantic-delegation authority and remain isolated formal/reference future-generation semantics, never changes to the deployed legacy generation.
- Preserve existing storage authentication bindings, original signer/object/QC/WAL identities and all retained delivery/source multiplicity except where an identity consequence is already explicitly entailed by an approved contract. New generation pins/hashes must be qualified; no old-object reinterpretation, migration, relabeling or resigning. No concrete sigma_next or other production deployment semantic value.
- F is forbidden. No factual-history observer, new trust/authority root, hidden source-domain restriction, invented source caps, loss/fault erasure, lineage truncation or replacement of missing bytes/history with successful callbacks, fixtures or downstream-success observations. The revised physical-cut claim remains explicit and is not evidence that the old physical-availability claim passed.
- Preserve fixed-epoch enrolled Snapshot Provenance Profile v1 authority and deployment boundaries: no unenrolled node, epoch change, trusted-volume compromise/rollback, network bootstrap, external entropy/source-of-truth service or universal backup format without a new explicit human decision.
- R1/R2.1/R2.2 stay CLOSED for their original domains. R2.3 stays OPEN until substantive implementation, proof, composition and required reviews succeed. Named DeltaReduce.nativeArithmeticRecoveryRefines begins only after substantive reviewed R2.3 closure. Full R3 remains forbidden. No conditional refinement may be portrayed as production GO.
- No sorry, hidden/circular/public-success axioms, vacuous theorem/domain weakening, opaque accept callbacks, prevalidated-success assumptions or relabeled FAIL/NO_GO. Requalify every affected source/model/refinement/mutant/compatibility/review gate required by the selected semantics. Sequential process reviews are not independent Formal GO attestations.
- No new sprint, reimport, reset, manual graph advancement, fake RESUME/START for STOP, duplicate result/review, nginx-qa patch/deploy/restart, subagents, foreign-file changes or frozen-ref rewrites unless separately and explicitly authorized for infrastructure maintenance. Preserve execution/audit history and healthy unrelated services. ACK changes scope authorization/audit only and never advances the graph, completes an assignment, approves a review or bypasses another gate.
- The previously selected EC-SOURCE-STEP-v1 semantics remain authoritative. The orchestrator may compose the minimum isolated formal/reference EC persistence/durability/source-association contract under the standing R2.3 delegation, including canonical bytes, source relations, append/barrier/commit/expose semantics and incomplete/crash/replay interpretation. This does not authorize a production WAL kind, production storage encoding, W1 extension, runtime producer change, new trust root or legacy-history conformance claim.
- Seed evidence verifier/derivation selection, implementation and proof are delegated only within the current standing R2.3 semantic-delegation authority. The orchestrator may select and implement the minimal deterministic formal/reference verifier and seed derivation contract using already approved authority, original evidence and fixed context. No implicit reuse of NSG1 as a beacon protocol is permitted unless its already approved semantics explicitly cover that use.
- A new Pending decision is still mandatory before introducing a new trust/authority root, independently trusted key source, signing authority, beacon/entropy authority, factual-history observer, external oracle or other independent source of truth; before weakening validator/epoch authentication; before narrowing the lawful source/admissible-history domain; before changing deployed production semantics, production Init/Next, production WAL/storage encoding or runtime behavior; before changing existing certificate/QC/signature/WAL/original-object identity beyond consequences already entailed by approved contracts; before choosing concrete production seed/private-key/arithmetic/sigma values; before weakening any safety, determinism, provenance, compatibility, recovery, review or Formal GO gate; or before entering full R3.
- The orchestrator must not silently repurpose an existing authority whose approved contract does not cover the required use. Applicability of an existing key, validator authority, storage authority or configuration authority must be explicit and source-bound.
- Dependent R2.3 composition may continue after each delegated contract has been explicitly recorded, implemented, proved and passed its applicable ordinary review/qualification gates. No additional Pending decision is required merely to select another minimal deterministic formal/reference binding, persistence association, verifier, derivation rule, provenance relation or history-association rule that stays inside the standing delegation envelope.
- Every delegated semantic choice must remain explicit, immutable-source-bound and auditable, including exact source inputs, selected rule, materially relevant alternatives, rationale, compatibility consequences and affected qualification. It must not be hidden as a theorem premise, helper definition, trusted callback, fixture assumption or prevalidated input.
- If multiple solutions satisfy the delegated envelope, select the minimal deterministic solution that introduces the least new semantics, reuses the greatest amount of already approved authority and canonical representation, preserves the largest lawful source/history domain and adds the smallest isolated formal/reference surface.
- The standing delegation itself is not evidence that R2.3 is correct or closed and is not Formal GO. Component PASS, process review, scope application or ACK likewise does not establish closure.
- After substantive reviewed R2.3 closure, continue the already authorized DeltaReduce.nativeArithmeticRecoveryRefines, its axiom audit and applicable formal/refinement/mutant/compatibility/qualification gates. Production integration and full R3 remain outside this authority.

Existing execution, review and qualification gates remain unchanged. This effective instruction supersedes conflicting historical scope text.

